post.description:
Create new Node or file. Maximum file size: 100MB for regular uploads, 2GB when using chunking technique.

For files larger than 100MB, use the chunking technique:

1. Split the file into chunks (recommended: 15MB per chunk)
2. Upload each chunk to: POST /api/v2/{customer_id}/file_uploads/upload_chunk
   Required parameters (FormData):
   - data[attributes][file]: The chunk blob
   - data[attributes][file-id]: Unique file ID (format: customer_id.uuid.filename)
   - data[attributes][original-filename]: Original file name
   - data[attributes][part]: Chunk number (starting from 1)
   - data[attributes][uuid]: Unique UUID for each chunk

3. After all chunks are uploaded, merge them: POST /api/v2/{customer_id}/file_uploads/confirm_upload
   Required parameters (FormData):
   - data[attributes][file-id]: The same file ID used during chunk upload
   - data[attributes][uuid]: A unique UUID for the merge request
   - data[attributes][original-filename]: Original file name

4. Use the returned file-path or file-url in the DMS nodes creation request

JavaScript Example:
```javascript
// Helper function to generate UUID
function uuidv4() {
  return 'xxxxxxxx-xxxx-4xxx-yxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx'.replace(/[xy]/g, function(c) {
    const r = Math.random() * 16 | 0, v = c == 'x' ? r : (r & 0x3 | 0x8);
    return v.toString(16);
  });
}

// Step 1: Initialize chunking parameters
const CHUNK_SIZE = 15 * 1024 * 1024; // 15MB
const file = document.querySelector('input[type="file"]').files[0];
const totalChunks = Math.ceil(file.size / CHUNK_SIZE);
const fileId = `${customerId}.${uuidv4()}.${file.name.replace(/\s|\(|\)/g, '')}`;
const mergeUuid = uuidv4();

// Step 2: Upload each chunk sequentially
for (let i = 0; i < totalChunks; i++) {
  const start = i * CHUNK_SIZE;
  const end = Math.min(start + CHUNK_SIZE, file.size);
  const chunk = file.slice(start, end);

  const formData = new FormData();
  formData.append('data[attributes][file]', chunk);
  formData.append('data[attributes][file-id]', fileId);
  formData.append('data[attributes][original-filename]', file.name);
  formData.append('data[attributes][part]', i + 1);
  formData.append('data[attributes][uuid]', uuidv4());

  const response = await fetch(`/api/v2/${customerId}/file_uploads/upload_chunk`, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${apiKey}` },
    body: formData
  });

  if (!response.ok) {
    throw new Error(`Chunk ${i + 1} upload failed`);
  }
}

// Step 3: Merge all chunks
const mergeFormData = new FormData();
mergeFormData.append('data[attributes][file-id]', fileId);
mergeFormData.append('data[attributes][uuid]', mergeUuid);
mergeFormData.append('data[attributes][original-filename]', file.name);

const mergeResponse = await fetch(`/api/v2/${customerId}/file_uploads/confirm_upload`, {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${apiKey}` },
  body: mergeFormData
});

const mergeData = await mergeResponse.json();
const filePath = mergeData.data.attributes['file-path'];
const fileUrl = mergeData.data.attributes['file-url'];

// Step 4: Create DMS node with the uploaded file
const dmsFormData = new FormData();
dmsFormData.append('data[attributes][name]', file.name);
dmsFormData.append('data[attributes][file][link]', filePath);
dmsFormData.append('data[attributes][file][name]', file.name);
dmsFormData.append('data[attributes][file][file-content-type]', file.type);

const dmsResponse = await fetch(`/api/v2/${customerId}/projects/${projectId}/dms/nodes`, {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${apiKey}` },
  body: dmsFormData
});

const dmsNode = await dmsResponse.json();
console.log('DMS Node created:', dmsNode);
```

put.description:
Updates a specific list by its id. This endpoint uses a draft-based workflow that requires 3 sequential requests with the same temp-uuid:

**Step 1 - Initialize draft:** Send `init_draft: true` with a client-generated `temp-uuid` to copy existing entries into a draft table.

**Step 2 - Modify entries:** Send one or more requests with the same `temp-uuid` to add, update, or delete entries in the draft.
- To add/update an entry: include an `item` object with `name`, `uuid`, `parent-id`, and `order`.
- To delete an entry: include `entry-uuid` with the UUID of the entry to remove.

**Step 3 - Save changes:** Send `save: true` with the same `temp-uuid` to persist the draft changes to the actual list.

The `temp-uuid` must be a valid UUID and unique for each update session. It is generated by the client.

---

**curl Examples:**

**Step 1 — Initialize draft:**
<pre>
curl -X PUT "https://app.planradar.com/api/v2/{customer_id}/lists/{list_id}" \
  -H "X-PlanRadar-API-Key: YOUR_API_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "data": {
      "attributes": {
        "temp-uuid": "c7982fd2-cf0c-4806-a3ef-f87447e80e5f",
        "init_draft": true
      }
    }
  }'
</pre>

**Step 2 — Add a new entry:**
<pre>
curl -X PUT "https://app.planradar.com/api/v2/{customer_id}/lists/{list_id}" \
  -H "X-PlanRadar-API-Key: YOUR_API_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "data": {
      "attributes": {
        "temp-uuid": "c7982fd2-cf0c-4806-a3ef-f87447e80e5f",
        "item": {
          "name": "New Entry",
          "uuid": "5101ebd3-922c-4830-85aa-b7b6be97d2ca",
          "parent-id": null,
          "order": 0
        }
      }
    }
  }'
</pre>

**Step 3 — Save changes:**
<pre>
curl -X PUT "https://app.planradar.com/api/v2/{customer_id}/lists/{list_id}" \
  -H "X-PlanRadar-API-Key: YOUR_API_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "data": {
      "attributes": {
        "temp-uuid": "c7982fd2-cf0c-4806-a3ef-f87447e80e5f",
        "save": true
      }
    }
  }'
</pre>

post.description:
This API is used for creating a ticket type.
       <br />
       <b>Example:</b>
       <br />

        {
        "data": {
          "attributes": {
            "name": "tickettypeone",
            "capabilities": {
              "has-media": true,
              "has-plan-position": true,
              "store-geolocation-data": false,
              "has-comments": false,
              "has-due-date-extension": true,
              "has-recurring-reminders": false,
              "has-signature": true,
              "has-locking": true,
              "has_sign_as_someone_else": true
            },
            "typed-fields": {
              "bda0b598-ddbf-48c8-8da5-60d2c5983e89": {
                "name": "fieldname",
                "type": "CustomFields::IntegerType",
                "order": 1,
                "visible-to": ["xmy","yen","lwm","lm","yn"],
                "editable-by": ["xmy","yen","lwm","lm"]
              }
            },
            "static-fields": {
              "progress": {
                "order": 1,
                "visible-to": ["xmy","yen","lwm","lm","yn"],
                "editable-by": ["xmy","yen","lwm","lm","yn"]
              }
            },
            "form-decorators":{
                "b6cd699b-668f-4360-b6ac-5de4404a094b":{
                    "name":"seperator",
                    "visible-to":[
                        762, "lm"
                    ],
                    "order":2,
                    "type":"FormDecorators::Separator",
                    "description": "",
                    "check-all-roles": false,
                    "default_value": "",
                    "required": false
                },"b6cd699b-668f-4360-b6ac-5de4404a095b":{
                    "name":"group",
                    "order":3,
                    "type":"FormDecorators::Group",
                    "description": "",
                    "visible_to": [],
                    "check_all_roles": true,
                    "fields":[
                        "cc376c7d-054a-4901-98bb-4069d4e4aa74",
                        "cc376c0d-054a-4901-98bb-4069d4e4aa74",
                        "parent-id"
                    ]
                }
            }
          }
        }
      }

       <br /><br />
       <b>CheckListType Field Example:</b>
       <br />
       The CheckListType field provides a checklist with configurable response options, attachments, and notes.
       <br /><br />
       <b>Configuration Options:</b>
       <ul>
         <li><b>response-label</b>: Display labels for responses. Valid values: 1 (Yes/No/N/A), 2 (True/False/N/A), 3 (Pass/Fail/N/A). Default: 1</li>
         <li><b>response-color</b>: Color scheme for responses. Valid values: 1 (Green/Red/Blue), 2 (Red/Green/Blue), 3 (Blue for all). Default: 1</li>
         <li><b>enable-attachments</b>: Enable attachment support. Default: true</li>
         <li><b>max-attachments</b>: Maximum attachments per item (requires enable-attachments: true). Default: 1</li>
         <li><b>required-attachments-for</b>: Require attachments for specific answers (requires enable-attachments: true AND max-attachments set). Valid values: [1, 2, 3]</li>
         <li><b>enable-notes</b>: Enable notes for checklist items. Default: true</li>
         <li><b>required-notes-for</b>: Require notes for specific answers (requires enable-notes: true). Valid values: [1, 2, 3]</li>
       </ul>
       <br />
       <b>Answer Values:</b>
       <ul>
         <li><b>1</b>: First response option (Yes/True/Pass depending on response-label)</li>
         <li><b>2</b>: Second response option (No/False/Fail depending on response-label)</li>
         <li><b>3</b>: Third response option (N/A for all response-labels)</li>
       </ul>
       <br />
       <b>conditional-config for CheckListType:</b>
       <ul>
         <li><b>answered</b>: Field has any response (no values required)</li>
         <li><b>not_answered</b>: Field has no response (no values required)</li>
         <li><b>includes_any</b>: Response matches any of the specified values (values required: [1, 2, 3])</li>
         <li><b>includes_all</b>: Response matches all specified values (values required: [1, 2, 3])</li>
       </ul>
       <br />
       <b>Full CheckListType Example:</b>
       <br />

        {
        "data": {
          "attributes": {
            "name": "Safety Inspection Form",
            "capabilities": {
              "has-media": true,
              "has-plan-position": true
            },
            "typed-fields": {
              "checklist-field-uuid": {
                "name": "Safety Checklist",
                "type": "CustomFields::CheckListType",
                "order": 1,
                "visible-to": ["lm", "yn"],
                "editable-by": ["lm"],
                "response-label": 1,
                "response-color": 1,
                "enable-attachments": true,
                "max-attachments": 3,
                "required-attachments-for": [1, 2],
                "enable-notes": true,
                "required-notes-for": [2, 3]
              },
              "conditional-text-field-uuid": {
                "name": "Additional Notes",
                "type": "CustomFields::ShortTextType",
                "order": 2,
                "visible-to": ["lm"],
                "editable-by": ["lm"],
                "conditional-config": {
                  "condition-type": "any",
                  "conditions": {
                    "checklist-field-uuid": {
                      "predicate": "includes_any",
                      "values": [1, 2]
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }

       <br /><br />
       <b>Minimal CheckListType (uses defaults):</b>
       <br />

        {
        "typed-fields": {
          "checklist-field-uuid": {
            "name": "Quick Checklist",
            "type": "CustomFields::CheckListType",
            "order": 1,
            "visible-to": ["lm"],
            "editable-by": ["lm"]
          }
        }
      }

put.description:
This API is used for updating multiple tickets at once based on the provided filteration. However, no filter will update all the data of the project.
      <br />
      <b>Filtering </b>
      You can filter the tickets by one of your created filters by providing its id to the apply_filter attribute.
      Moreover, the tickets can be filtered based on any condition of the related model. These have to be set in the filter object of the body.
      Multiple filters can be used at the same time.
      <br />
      Example:
      <br />

      {
        "apply_filter":"mod",
        "filter":{
           "uuid":[
              {
                 "predicate":"in",
                 "value":[
                    "b404f669-e02a-4273-bcff-aac72b31386f",
                    "fa30521c-bf68-4246-b50f-29fd9c91ee5f"
                 ]
              }
           ]
        },
        "data":{
           "attributes":{
              "priority-id":"ol"
           },
           "obk":{
              "tf37e04757dabbca63":"4",
              "tf7ae8b29ea4b4c1e9":[
                 "makw"
              ],
              "typed-values-metadata":{
                 "tf37e04757dabbca63":{
                    "note":"observation details",
                    "has_attachments":true
                 }
              }
           }
        }
     }

      <br /><br />
      <b>CheckList Fields in Batch Update</b><br />
      When updating CheckList fields (CustomFields::CheckListType), typed-values-metadata must be placed inside the ticket_type_id bucket alongside the typed values. The server extracts it automatically.<br />
      <b>Silent Skip Behavior:</b> If a checklist field requires a mandatory note or attachment and the metadata is not provided, the checklist field update is silently skipped for that ticket. Other fields in the same batch update are still applied normally.

